This directory vendors a slice of the official WebAssembly conformance
test suite, unmodified, for use by the `wasm-conformance` crate (see
`code/specs/W05-wasm-conformance-harness.md`).

Source:        https://github.com/WebAssembly/testsuite
Pinned commit: 28864811cf03bdbf880733786148feaba339582d
Fetched:       2026-08-13
Fetch method:  code/packages/rust/wasm-conformance/tests/fixtures/fetch_testsuite.py

The pinned commit was resolved via:
    git ls-remote https://github.com/WebAssembly/testsuite.git refs/heads/main

`main` is a live, moving branch that interleaves post-MVP proposal files
(GC, exceptions, tail calls, SIMD, threads/atomics) with plain WASM 1.0
MVP-core ones, so a pinned SHA -- not `main` itself -- is vendored to keep
this repo's conformance baseline reproducible across re-fetches. Bumping
the pin is a deliberate, reviewed decision, not something a re-run of the
fetch script does casually.

Only the WASM 1.0 MVP-core `.wast` files are vendored here; see
`code/specs/W05-wasm-conformance-harness.md` section 6 for the full list
of what's deliberately excluded from this initial slice (SIMD, threads,
exceptions, tail calls, GC/reference-types beyond this repo's existing
narrow slice, memory64, the component model, and files needing the
`spectest` host-import module) and why each becomes its own future
phase's vendored slice.

